# Inbox and reads

Source: `R2App` (`ITEMS`, `visibleItems`, `ack`, `snoozed`, `snooze`,
`inboxRows`, `sel`, `startRead`, `recheck`, `toGo`). Chunk: C30.

## Inbox

- Tabs All / Needs action / Updates / Snoozed with counts. Rows: severity
  (colour + icon + word), title, product, source line ("API keys · cached",
  "rotated 07:46"), when, acknowledged mark. Selecting opens the detail pane:
  body, facts table, "Why this matters" explanation, action button (navigates
  with context), Acknowledge / Mark as needing action, Snooze or Unsnooze.
- Empty states distinguish "first read pending" from "nothing needs action"
  and name partial sources ("3 of 6 sources were read at 07:45").
- Snooze: per item, core-computed return time, 24 hours for every item in
  P09 (the prototype's deadline-bound rotation snooze is not carried: no
  admitted operation has a grace deadline, P20). The label, toast and
  Snoozed-tab "Returns …" text all state the same time (I11). The
  `deadline` field stays optional for a future item that has a real one.
- Contextual navigation: an item's action carries a target (screen, product,
  tab, conversation). Into an ended conversation it sets a transient hint
  offering "Open the saved transcript" and "Start a new investigation".

## Reads (I4)

- `readTenant` runs a finite read of every selected product; `ReadStatus`
  carries per-product state (pending, ok, partial, needsRole), last-read
  time and counts. First read on a fresh tenant shows pending everywhere.
- Completion toast: ok "Read finished at 07:45 · all sources complete" or
  warn "· 3 sources partial"; for fresh tenants "· 1 product still needs a
  role" or "· no activity yet in <tenant>". `recheckProduct` after a role is
  granted shows an info toast and re-reads.

## Core contract

- Scope `InboxItem{id, kind, severity, title, product, source, when, body,
  facts, action_target, explanation, deadline?, snooze_return?, acknowledged}`
  per tenant; intents `acknowledgeItem`, `snoozeItem`, `unsnoozeItem`,
  `readTenant`, `recheckProduct`.
- The rotation reminder (`rotation-<application>`) is a distinct item id from
  the expiry alert and clears only when the old key's deletion is read back
  (I7). Items exist only for admitted products (DESIGN-V2 §6).

## Fixtures and tests

- Board R2Inbox. Tests V2-R02, R04, R08, R09; V2-T04, T12, T13; V2-N02.
# P09 re-cut: port the prototype, one gate per screen

Agreed with the owner on 2026-10-29 after C32 took twenty review rounds while
the built v2 screens never matched the design. This supersedes the chunking
of C33–C34 in `IMPLEMENTATION-PLAN.md`; the specification
(`docs/architecture/ui-v2/`) and the core work of C27–C33 stand.

## The bar

- **The prototype is the spec.** `docs/architecture/ui-v2/prototype/` (Refined
  Native v2, version 134, checksums in `MANIFEST.sha256`) is the reference for
  every screen; the canvas is not consulted.
- **A screen is done when it matches its board.** Side by side at 1440 wide in
  light and dark (the board is drawn at 1440×900; where the display cannot
  give a 900px web area both sides are rendered at the window's measured web
  area, named in the composite's caption, 1440×800 on the current Mac), with
  real core data wired, and the fast checks (typecheck,
  Vitest, the affected Rust suites) passing. Parity is structural: regions,
  widths, spacing, type scale, tokens and component shapes. Content differs;
  accessibility corrections (focus rings, contrast, status regions) may deviate
  and are noted. The owner judges each composite.
- **Composites** live at `docs/planning/evidence/<chunk>/parity/<board>-<theme>.png`
  (prototype left, app right) with `notes.md` listing deviations, produced by
  `tools/parity/compose.py` (headless render of the prototype board beside the
  fixture app's own capture).
- **One heavy gate per chunk**, after the owner's parity approval: rebuild,
  native acceptance, the full Rust fixture suite and the Codex review, accepted
  at **8**. The phase review (after C44) is **9**; the C29 live Vulture row runs
  before it once the owner designates the L19 family.
- **No legacy views inside v2.** Each screen is new components over the
  existing core intents and `ShellSnapshot`; the legacy feature components stay
  untouched for the legacy shell until C44 removes it.
- **Cadence.** The shell is approved before any screen inside it. After that
  a chunk's composite is posted and work moves to the next chunk; the owner's
  notes are applied as they arrive.

## Chunks

