|---|---|---|
| R1 the stacked list card collapsed to a line at 900×600 / 200% (`min-height: 0`, `overflow: hidden` inside a shrinkable grid row) | When the cards stack (below 1280 CSS px) the grid no longer shares a bounded height: its rows are each card's own height, the list card keeps between 240 CSS px and half the viewport (its tab panel scrolls inside it) and the page scrolls past both cards. Wide, the two-column grid is unchanged. | `apps/desktop/src/styles/tokens.css` (the `<1280px` block) |
| R2 the native layout predicate accepted the collapsed card; keyboard testing happened before resizing, from a programmatic focus, on an already selected detail | Every layout tree is now measured for the list card's usability (`list_usable`): at least 160 CSS px tall at its zoom, with the filter tabs, the first row and the footer inside the card's own frame. At every layout (1440 wide, 900×600 at 200%, both themes) the keyboard is driven again (`keyboard_at`): Tab from Read now reaches a tab and then a row; a row the detail does not show is focused (it is scrolled into the viewport, asserted against the window frame) and Enter changes the detail to it. An expiring API key (`keyExpiresInDays=5.5`) gives the second row. | `tools/native-acceptance/acceptance_c37.py`; `docs/architecture/native-checks.json` C37-N02 |
| E1 the gate's composites showed an unselected detail | The native script captures the composites itself from the populated state with the first row opened, bound to the gate bundle; the gate chain no longer captures separately. The owner judges the new composites before attempt-02 runs. | `acceptance_c37.py` (`composite`), `evidence/C37/parity/notes.md` |
| E2 the failed, partial and role-issue states were registered but not exercised natively | Before the populated read the script now drives the failed first read (every source answering 500, the API keys source through a new `apiKeysStatus` mode of the synthetic plane, since the runtime read counts as landed while its keys source reads: the empty state names the failed read) and a product needing a role (the sessions chart answering 403: Open role issue offered, the footer's partial coverage line, and the issue opening AI Runtime Security in Administration), each with its tree and capture retained. The registered text names exactly these branches. | `acceptance_c37.py` (N01), `tools/native-acceptance/mgmt_server.py` (`apiKeysStatus`), `native-checks.json` C37-N01 |

